{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SPLIT DONE — and the split is already vindicated.\n\n  * [rebar:f2f3-9cb1-335b-4e31] S1 — extract the retry/error cluster out of `transport.py`\n    (behaviour-preserving; forced by the 789/800 cap). **PASSED plan review FIRST TRY.** This\n    ticket took TEN rounds; S1 took one. That is the evidence the ten rounds were structural, not\n    a wording problem — the same result J9 -> J10 produced earlier in this epic.\n  * [rebar:6758-26b8-c9ea-4c5d] S2 — the 429 policy in the extracted module.\n\nS2 `depends_on` S1 as a REAL LINK, not prose: verified functionally, `next-batch` withholds S2\nwhile S1 is open (the available pool grew from 3 to 4 with S1 added and S2 excluded).\n\nBOTH WERE RETYPED FROM story TO task. `next-batch` reports a childless story as\nNEEDS_PLANNING, so as stories they would never have been offered as workable — the split would\nhave looked done while changing nothing.\n\nTHIS TICKET'S DESCRIPTION IS NOW A PARENT/DECOMPOSITION PLAN. The 28k-char implementation plan\nmoved into the children, which is where it belongs; this ticket's ACs are now about decomposition\ncompleteness and are checkable from the ticket graph. The ten-round review record stays here as\ncomments so the reason for the split is recoverable.\n\nREVIEW STATE: the rewritten plan returned BLOCK with ONE finding — that S2 left the\n`_paged_search` opt-in shape ambiguous (round 10's finding 2, which I had carried forward as an AC\nDEMANDING disambiguation rather than making the decision). Now decided in S2: `_paged_search`\nACCEPTS AND FORWARDS `rate_limit_retry: bool = False`; an unconditional `True` would silently grant\nretry to every future caller, which is the same inherit-by-omission hazard the per-call opt-in\nexists to prevent. NEXT ACTION: re-run `rebar review-plan b586-2fda-8a15-4260`, then claim this\nticket (the parent-first cascade needs it in_progress before S1 can be claimed).\n\nALSO ANSWERED, from round 10's open list: cap exhaustion must raise `BackendHTTPError(code=429)`,\nnever a raw `JIRAError` — that is what `_as_backend_http_error` already does and what J10's neutral\nexception contract exists to protect. And `_paged_search` DOES route through `_call_logged`,\nverified on `origin/main` post-9263 (round 10 could only assert it from plan text)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785617567828726001,"uuid":"570e3d54-da2d-41e2-b9ad-d65621061f04"}